From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov7251: the enable GPIO is optional

On the PICO 4 the four OV7251 tracking cameras share their shutdown line
(and their standby line); the board switches it once for all of them, so no
sensor can own it. Without the GPIO the driver leaves the line to the board
(gpiod_set_value_cansleep() accepts a NULL descriptor).
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
index 311c61d9e25d..fa5c96e1683e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
@@ -1680,7 +1680,7 @@ static int ov7251_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return PTR_ERR(ov7251->analog_regulator);
 	}
 
-	ov7251->enable_gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	ov7251->enable_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
 	if (IS_ERR(ov7251->enable_gpio)) {
 		dev_err(dev, "cannot get enable gpio\n");
 		return PTR_ERR(ov7251->enable_gpio);
